# Admin grid (list pages)

Every admin **index/list** page must use the abstract grid system — never hand-roll `<table class="admin-table">` markup.

Follow `docs/add-admin-section.md` §6.

## Required stack

1. Repository implements `ProvidesAdminGrid` with `gridDefinition()`, `countForGrid()`, `listForGrid()`.
2. Controller `index()` uses `GridRunner::fetch()` and passes `'grid' => $grid` to Twig.
3. Twig is only: `{% include 'components/grid.twig' with {grid: grid} %}` (+ optional callouts above the grid).

## Actions: mass **or** row column — never both

Grids use **one** action model:

| Model | UI | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Mass actions** (preferred for list CRUD) | Checkboxes + mass-action bar | Delete, block, publish, etc. on many rows |
| **Actions column** (`type: actions`) | Per-row Edit/Delete links | Only when there is **no** `massActions()` |

**Do not** combine `->massActions(...)` with an `actions` column. Edit opens via a **link** column (e.g. name/title → detail page). Delete (and similar) goes through mass actions + checkboxes.

Mass actions require:

- `->massActions('/admin/…/mass', [...])` on `GridDefinition`
- `POST /admin/…/mass` route + controller `mass()` → `runMassActions()`
- i18n: `confirm_mass_*`, `mass_done`

Rows that must not be bulk-selected (e.g. system Super role) set `'can_mass' => false`.

## Non-numeric row IDs

When `idField` is not numeric (e.g. role `slug`), set `->massIdType('string')`.
